{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Robot Voice",
 "category": "Effects",
 "text": "Sound: a buzzing, metallic robot 'talking' in random syllables: the vocoder-ish robot of electro and sci-fi.\n\nHow it's built: a buzzy pulse, ring-modulated by a sine for the metallic edge, through the State-Variable filter's band-pass; a Sample & Hold, ticked by a Clock's 1/16, jumps the CUTOFF to a new random 'vowel' on every syllable, and an envelope retriggered by the same clock chops it into syllables. One voice.\n\nPlay: hold a note and it talks on that pitch; change notes to change its voice.\n\nTweak: the clock's TEMPO (how fast it talks), the filter's CV and RESONANCE (how different the vowels are), the ring mod's MIX.",
